{
  "repo": "EH3D-ISOCAM",
  "ecosystem": "eh3d",
  "tagline": "The copper of a layer, offset exactly, as paths of the tools.",
  "description": "EH3D-ISOCAM is a Rust library and command line that read a Gerber layer, draw its copper on a fine grid, trace the paths of one or several isolation milling tools at the exact distance, remove the leftover copper, choose the direction and the order of the cuts and write them as G-code or HP-GL; it also reads and writes drill and outline files, lays a board out for both sides and a panel, and checks the design rules; it can also lay a path along gaps the tool does not fit in, scale and correct the work from reference points, write the openings of the solder mask and draw a preview of the passes. It has no window yet.",
